{"key": "5bfae215e2b674f3", "role": "operator", "t": 1790972904.638, "seconds": 6.185, "output": "```python\nimport json\n\ndef check_similarity(PURPOSE, Entity):\n    # Check if inputs are strings\n    if isinstance(PURPOSE, str) and isinstance(Entity, str):\n        # If both are strings, check if they are equal\n        if PURPOSE == Entity:\n            return 1\n        else:\n            return 0\n    \n    # Check if inputs are JSON tuples (lists in Python)\n    elif isinstance(PURPOSE, list) and isinstance(Entity, list):\n        # If both are lists, check if they have the same elements\n        if set(PURPOSE) == set(Entity):\n            return 1\n        else:\n            return 0\n    \n    # If inputs are neither strings nor lists, return 0\n    else:\n        return 0\n\n# Test the function\nPURPOSE = \"test\"\nEntity = \"test\"\nprint(check_similarity(PURPOSE, Entity))\n\nPURPOSE = json.dumps([\"test\", \"entity\"])\nEntity = json.dumps([\"test\", \"entity\"])\nprint(check_similarity(json.loads(PURPOSE), json.loads(Entity)))\n```"}
{"key": "bb04e8f3ea1b6777", "role": "operator", "t": 1790972904.642, "seconds": 6.19, "output": "```python\ndef check_similarity(PURPOSE, Date):\n    # Assuming the condition is that both PURPOSE and Date are not empty and have some similarity\n    if PURPOSE and Date:\n        # For simplicity, let's assume similarity means they have at least one common word\n        purpose_words = set(PURPOSE.split())\n        date_words = set(Date.split())\n        if purpose_words.intersection(date_words):\n            return 1\n    return 0\n\n# Test the function\nPURPOSE = \"Meeting Report\"\nDate = \"Meeting Schedule\"\nprint(check_similarity(PURPOSE, Date))\n```"}
